{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy","id":1458960,"title":"What do vampires know ,if anything, about the Technocracy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-05T23:36:48-07:00","id":1458960,"title":"What do vampires know ,if anything, about the Technocracy?","content":"So the Technocrats know a bit about vampires and have some information on their society and dealings etc. What do the vampires know about the Technocracy in return?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T00:03:39-07:00","id":1458961,"title":"","content":"Most vampires don't know anything. A few might realize that there are other conspiracies in the world and might even realize there's a business conspiracy (Syndicate) or one in the media (New World Order) but they'd probably have no idea those conspiracies were all separate heads of a singular hydra. Only maybe older Tremere or vampires who used to be mages or themselves Technocrats are likely to have anything approaching a full understanding of the Technocracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T03:45:31-07:00","id":1458982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mezlabor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy#post1458960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Technocrats know a bit about vampires and have some information on their society and dealings etc. What do the vampires know about the Technocracy in return?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere know there's a society of Mages that used reason and science to hunt mages but they're probably thinking about the Order of Reason not the Union.<br /> <br /> SOMEONE nuked Ravnos but I suspect even the most informed vampires have no idea who that is.<br /> <br /> Vampires are easily the most ignorant supernatural other than Hunters and even that's questionable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T06:50:39-07:00","id":1458998,"title":"","content":"I reckon the Tremere probably do decent book keeping and have someone somewhere keeping tabs and thus probably aren't more than 30 years out of date. The same may be true with the Nosferatu. However, having the books somewhere doesn't mean everyone bothers to read them or knows that they're even there (though I think it's really undersold how long vampires live for and how empty the latter part of their nights are, so I think it'd be a bit weird if a chantry/warren didn't have someone who read up on stuff like this for entertainment.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T12:31:24-07:00","id":1459045,"title":"","content":"It's one of my favorite things about the Ventrue that some within the clan canonically believe in a conspiracy theory that someone out there is pushing back against them and their influence on the world, but they have no idea who.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T12:48:18-07:00","id":1459050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1459045#post1459045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's one of my favorite things about the Ventrue that some within the clan canonically believe in a conspiracy theory that someone out there is pushing back against them and their influence on the world, but they have no idea who.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is interesting. I'm in a technocracy chronicle now where my syndicate media pop diva is in a business battle with a Ventrue over competing business interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T15:33:40-07:00","id":1459074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mezlabor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1459050#post1459050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is interesting. I'm in a technocracy chronicle now where my syndicate media pop diva is in a business battle with a Ventrue over competing business interests.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original Ventrue clanbook has a concept called the &quot;Secret Masters&quot;. The Secret Masters are supposed to be a secret coterie of incredible beings who manipulate everything behind the scenes to rule the world. The Ventrue work against them to keep the world free. It's a very high level Jyhad style concept. The Secret Masters are a disparate group. The Antedeluvians are supposed to be part of this, but it predates them (remember that the Ventrue antedeluvian is supposed to be dead and is not among their number, it's likely the Ventrue believe the Secret Masters are responsible for this destruction). The Incarna spirits, archmages, mummies, and any other powerful beings are included in their numbers.<br /> <br /> Basically anyone who opposes the Ventrue for reasons unknown to them are probably labelled as pawns of the Secret Masters. This includes the lupines, mages, Inquisition, Sabbat, and others. The Masters themselves are powerful supernatural forces. It's likely the concept and make up of them have changed over the millennia. Originally, they were probably powerful Incarna/Aeon level spirits, and the Ventrue added more of them over the years including very physical beings as part of the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> The name &quot;Secret Masters&quot; dates only to the 1700s, but before that they used many other names. This is likely a very, very, old concept among the concept because they trace it back to Caine informing Ventrue of their existence. As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11599\" data-vbnamecard=\"11599\">Reasor</a> stated, &quot;some&quot; Ventrue believe it. So the numbers of the Ventrue who buy into the concept, and what an individual Ventrue believes is true about them is all over the place. It's something an ST will need to define in her own chronicles.<br /> <br /> It's a combination of occult lore, bonkers conspiracy theory, misunderstood reality, and paranoid fantasy. It's never developed in any other sourcebook to my knowledge, so it is easily overlooked. It's very much a concept that is left to STs to develop it as they see fit. Just want it to be lunatic ravings? Then the Secret Masters don't exist. Want it to be a combination of real forces which don't actually work together as the Ventrue conceive? That works too. Want an actual group or groups of beings that actually fit the concept? Then it exists at least in some kind of format.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Technocracy is likely NOT considered to be members of the Secret Masters, who seem to have a distinct umbral nature. The first Venture clanbook explicitly states that while mages are manipulated by the Secret Masters that those who deal with science &quot;remain free&quot; of them. In that sense, the Ventrue would like view the Technocracy as uneasy allies against the Secret Masters. This does not mean the Technocracy is seen as trustworthy or friendly. Just that they - like the Ventrue - are one of the few groups free of their influence.<br /> <br /> The original Ventrue clanbook was written by Andrew Greenberg at the very beginning of Rob Hatch's run as Vampire 2e developer. And it fits some of the more gonzo crossover stuff that defined Greenberg's earlier run as Vampire developer. As such, it's not surprising the concept never gets mentioned again as the Vampire game toned down anything associated with the Umbra, the other game lines, and restricted the game's themes to sect conflicts between vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> At the time I first read the Ventrue clanbook, I admit I scratched my head a lot after reading about it. However, I've grown to like the concept and have worked to develop ways I can meaningfully incorporate it into my chronicles both as an element within the clan, and as something that viably intersects with the wider game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T15:42:58-07:00","id":1459075,"title":"","content":"There's probably more than a few &quot;friend of a friend&quot; stories among vampires about Men in Black (as in the subjects of traditional UFO and/or conspiracy folklore), conspiracies of the living wealthy elite, and the like. Probably most consider them some sort of modern government version of the Society of Leopold/Inquisition from the old days. (And if you use the Second Inquisition, then there is such a thing.) Some, especially older or more well read Tremere, may think they could be descendants of forces the Order encountered before they became vampires. But an organization of reality manipulating wizards pretending to be scientists is likely to be considered too much to believe. <br /> Such is my take, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T18:31:37-07:00","id":1459086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mezlabor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy#post1458960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Technocrats know a bit about vampires and have some information on their society and dealings etc. What do the vampires know about the Technocracy in return?</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends a lot.<br /> <br /> First of all, the idea that the World of Darkness\u2122 is a cohesive setting simply isn't true. There was a lot of back and forth in this arena through the years, but ultimately each line is its own thing, give or take a few references and the odd crossover book, and whatever is true for one have no bearing on the other.<br /> <br /> What it means for this question is that a) they avoid talking about other Denizens at length in any particular line and b) the perception on the matter varies a lot between readers as we all have to read in the subtext, and dominion over each line affects the outcome.<br /> <br /> So we can't say for sure what to expect from your ST, even if you say your ST knows a lot of everything and is very consistent and orthodox.<br /> <br /> But my personal take on the matter would be:<br /> <br /> - The Nosferatu have the Shrecknet, the single most protected computer network in the setting. Depending on your understanding of some official material, it already withstood Awakened hackers more than once, including the Virtual Adepts. It would be hard for them to be completely unaware of the nature of whatever tried to get to them;<br /> - Still with the Nos, they are information dealers and have contacts far and wide. Obfuscate is also a pesky Discipline to get through, not so much because it is hard to but because it is extremely counter-intuitive in the way it works, so few Mages would even try a working spell to see them. Nos hackers are likely among the people the VAs talk with and consider a part of their circles in the internet;<br /> - The Tremere used to be a Hermetic House, and several of their elders are still from that time. Indeed, even as vampires they stayed within the Order of Hermes for 200 years, leaving only in the beginning of the 13th century. They are extremely likely to still keep an eye on what's happening among the Mages, in the very least to avoid the OoH persecution in name of the still standing Massassa War;<br /> - It is also probable that from time to time a neonate is Embraced among Mages wanting immortality that badly or non-awakened associated with the Traditions, and then get fresh news on what's happening;<br /> - The Followers of Set had a long history with Mages in the past and are dealers of everything and anything in the present. This past information is important to them, and the present situation means that they are likely to come across absolutely any supernatural group with interesting offers, specially considering that, despite their tendency to seduce you to ever darker paths, the deals themselves are as good as they say;<br /> - Vampires are master conspirators entrenched in mortal institutions and with time on their sides. Not that the Union isn't, but where the Union have a broad scope the vampires have deep roots. It would be hard to never pass through their webs, even if left alone, and never be detected;<br /> - Age is also a huge boon. Even if a given vampire is new to the night, they're never too far from someone with at least a few centuries. More time to take on clues, more time to see strange things, more time to investigate, more time to spread influence and prepare, and usually a very good memory. With those guys the problem is that no matter what you think the game is, they've been playing this match before you were even born;<br /> - Disciplines aren't nearly as flexible as Magick by any stretch of the imagination, but they are potent and useful. Auspex 2 is enough to identify Mages on sight, easy to pull out and is a very common Discipline, almost half the Camarilla have it as in-clan. Dominate can control and read minds. And despite the lack of finesse, Presence is hugely potent on what it tries to do. Auspex may well be the single best information gathering effect in the entire WoD and the other two are no pushovers when it comes to making someone spill the beans;<br /> - Mages can be Ghouls, and some do this on purpose. Others are tricked into it. Some may come to it by accident (in the sense that the vampire didn't expected to get a Mage). Either way this puts a Mage directly under a vampire's influence, and them it is a matter of time before the vampire learn about the Mage and their society. Techies are just as likely to end up like this, and some appreciate the perks;<br /> - Finally, many vampires have mystic tendencies that would naturally drive them to the same places that Mages frequent. It isn't impossible that some gathering either of Traditions or Conventions have vampires in their midst, or at least a Ghoul. It isn't impossible that some long distance partners in whatever project a Mage or Techie have is a vampire. And while it may be rare, stretched through time it compounds.<br /> <br /> I'd say the chance of vampires being aware of the Technocracy are pretty high, at least to the same degree the Technocracy is aware of them. And individual vampires may know a pretty high amount of details on top of that. But it all ultimately depends on individuals and, more importantly, on your ST's views and plans.<br /> <br /> <b>Maybe this Toreador had a fairly important hand in putting you where you are today</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-06T21:11:53-07:00","id":1459095,"title":"","content":"My take on the subject is that every line is canon to the World of Darkness but only to an extent.<br /> <br /> After all, there's vampires, werewolves, and mages oh my in every line and they all do have an affect on each other.<br /> <br /> But nothing is 100% true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T20:57:49-07:00","id":1460108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1459095#post1459095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take on the subject is that every line is canon to the World of Darkness but only to an extent.<br /> <br /> After all, there's vampires, werewolves, and mages oh my in every line and they all do have an affect on each other.<br /> <br /> But nothing is 100% true.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal preference as usually been to pick which game is taking primary prominence (am I playing a Vampire game which involves mages or an I playing a Mage came which involves vampires, for example) and work from there, with the game I'm using taking precedence and anything from the other game being yes, no, or maybe as needed. (I have some vague recollection of someone from WWGS once telling me this was how the developers tended to approach their own game lines, at least during the late 2nd ed and revised periods.) Trying to do a game in which you are using two (or more) games, with their backstories, cosmologies and factions, at the same time is a lot more of a juggling act, but its certainly doable if you are willing to put in the effort. And part of that involves deciding which aspects of which game are true (or at least truer than the other). So if Vampire+Mage, then you have to decide just how powerful the Technocracy is, how much influence they wield, and how much of an interest do they take in the Kindred, as well as just how aware the Kindred are of them (elders, ancilla, and neonates likely having much different levels of awareness). <br /> <br /> In perfect hindsight, I kind of wish each game line had included an Antagonists sourcebook which included a chapter about other supernaturals (Vampire, for example, having one that had chapters about mortal threats, vampire threats, and then supernaturals such as lupines, demons, ghosts, etc. as the appear in Vampire and work in its cosmology/world view) and then specific crossover books for each line that talked about how and why those two groups might meet/clash, issues with rules or cosmology that are likely to come up and ways to handle them, and what each group is doing in the other's signature city (the Vampire/Werewolf one talking about ghoul or embraced werewolves, vampires astrally projecting into the Umbra, what ties if any the Beast has with the Wyrm, what information - and misinformation - each group has about the other, what werewolves are doing in Chicago, etc.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-15T23:00:14-07:00","id":1460112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1459074#post1459074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The original Ventrue clanbook has a concept called the &amp;quot;Secret Masters&amp;quot;. The Secret Masters are supposed to be a secret coterie of incredible beings who manipulate everything behind the scenes to rule the world. The Ventrue work against them to keep the world free. It's a very high level Jyhad style concept. The Secret Masters are a disparate group. The Antedeluvians are supposed to be part of this, but it predates them (remember that the Ventrue antedeluvian is supposed to be dead and is not among their number, it's likely the Ventrue believe the Secret Masters are responsible for this destruction). The Incarna spirits, archmages, mummies, and any other powerful beings are included in their numbers.<br /> <br /> Basically anyone who opposes the Ventrue for reasons unknown to them are probably labelled as pawns of the Secret Masters. This includes the lupines, mages, Inquisition, Sabbat, and others. The Masters themselves are powerful supernatural forces. It's likely the concept and make up of them have changed over the millennia. Originally, they were probably powerful Incarna/Aeon level spirits, and the Ventrue added more of them over the years including very physical beings as part of the conspiracy.<br /> <br /> The name &amp;quot;Secret Masters&amp;quot; dates only to the 1700s, but before that they used many other names. This is likely a very, very, old concept among the concept because they trace it back to Caine informing Ventrue of their existence. As <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> stated, &amp;quot;some&amp;quot; Ventrue believe it. So the numbers of the Ventrue who buy into the concept, and what an individual Ventrue believes is true about them is all over the place. It's something an ST will need to define in her own chronicles.<br /> <br /> It's a combination of occult lore, bonkers conspiracy theory, misunderstood reality, and paranoid fantasy. It's never developed in any other sourcebook to my knowledge, so it is easily overlooked. It's very much a concept that is left to STs to develop it as they see fit. Just want it to be lunatic ravings? Then the Secret Masters don't exist. Want it to be a combination of real forces which don't actually work together as the Ventrue conceive? That works too. Want an actual group or groups of beings that actually fit the concept? Then it exists at least in some kind of format.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Technocracy is likely NOT considered to be members of the Secret Masters, who seem to have a distinct umbral nature. The first Venture clanbook explicitly states that while mages are manipulated by the Secret Masters that those who deal with science &amp;quot;remain free&amp;quot; of them. In that sense, the Ventrue would like view the Technocracy as uneasy allies against the Secret Masters. This does not mean the Technocracy is seen as trustworthy or friendly. Just that they - like the Ventrue - are one of the few groups free of their influence.<br /> <br /> The original Ventrue clanbook was written by Andrew Greenberg at the very beginning of Rob Hatch's run as Vampire 2e developer. And it fits some of the more gonzo crossover stuff that defined Greenberg's earlier run as Vampire developer. As such, it's not surprising the concept never gets mentioned again as the Vampire game toned down anything associated with the Umbra, the other game lines, and restricted the game's themes to sect conflicts between vampires themselves.<br /> <br /> At the time I first read the Ventrue clanbook, I admit I scratched my head a lot after reading about it. However, I've grown to like the concept and have worked to develop ways I can meaningfully incorporate it into my chronicles both as an element within the clan, and as something that viably intersects with the wider game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question about the Ventrue: who are the Directorate? My\u2026 understanding is that they are the ruling council of Clan Ventrue, but I\u2019m not 100% sure about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-16T00:26:13-07:00","id":1460115,"title":"","content":"It's a little vague, but in general the Directorate is the clan leadership of the Ventrue. The Directorate are the elders of the Ventrue clan who meet to direct the clan's efforts. While every city has a &quot;Board&quot; of the Ventrue who reside there, there are Directorates that cover a greater geographical area. Thus you could take it to mean the leadership of the Ventrue within a particular city, a particular region, or the clan as a whole. I think it is currently in London where the clan meets for its overall leadership meetings. The local boards meet every first Tuesday of the month, but the greater directorates meet less frequently.<br /> <br /> It was originally mentioned in the Players Guide and later developed in the clanbooks. As such, details may vary between editions.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue generally decide things in a collective manner, a legacy of when the Ventrue antedeluvian was killed and its childer were forced to organized together for mutual protection at a time when the other antedeluvians were active. The exact name and format of these governing bodies are subject to change throughout history, but essentially serve the same purpose. While all Ventrue can attend and speak their mind, like everything in Vampire its the elders who truly decide things. Yet the Ventrue probably balance the ambitions of its younger members and the privileges of its elders better than most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-16T03:04:30-07:00","id":1460116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1460115#post1460115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little vague, but in general the Directorate is the clan leadership of the Ventrue. The Directorate are the elders of the Ventrue clan who meet to direct the clan's efforts. While every city has a &amp;quot;Board&amp;quot; of the Ventrue who reside there, there are Directorates that cover a greater geographical area. Thus you could take it to mean the leadership of the Ventrue within a particular city, a particular region, or the clan as a whole. I think it is currently in London where the clan meets for its overall leadership meetings. The local boards meet every first Tuesday of the month, but the greater directorates meet less frequently.<br /> <br /> It was originally mentioned in the Players Guide and later developed in the clanbooks. As such, details may vary between editions.<br /> <br /> The Ventrue generally decide things in a collective manner, a legacy of when the Ventrue antedeluvian was killed and its childer were forced to organized together for mutual protection at a time when the other antedeluvians were active. The exact name and format of these governing bodies are subject to change throughout history, but essentially serve the same purpose. While all Ventrue can attend and speak their mind, like everything in Vampire its the elders who truly decide things. Yet the Ventrue probably balance the ambitions of its younger members and the privileges of its elders better than most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-16T18:01:49-07:00","id":1460163,"title":"","content":"I'm generally anti-crossover, but assuming a crossover-positive universe...<br /> <br /> Vampires -- at least, the occultists -- know about mages. They may not know the <i>full</i> extent of mages' power, but they are aware mortals can and do learn <i>some</i> form of sorcery. And following from that, naturally, mages seem to have their own societies and version of the Masquerade. The exceedingly well-learned may be aware of a sectarian divide among mages, comparable to the Camarilla and Sabbat...and the mages' version of the Camarilla is known as the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Other than that, it's all going to be hearsay and telephone game-style vampiric urban legend.<br /> <br /> Maybe a strange mortal in a black suit showed up in Elysium, and was ushered into a back room with the Prince <i>immediately...</i>and not a word was said in polite company since. Maybe the Sabbat raided a chantry, thinking it was full of Tremere, only to be repelled with extreme prejudice by mortals wielding fire and lightning, with the scant survivors telling unbelievable tales of what they saw. Maybe an unfortunate lick tried feeding on a strange mortal, only to discover they had no blood at all but instead only bit down on a skeleton made of metal. Maybe the Tzimisce bishop whose hatred of mortals, and the depravities it inflicts upon them with great relish, is known throughout the sect...and then one night out of nowhere, they clear their entire evening schedule just to have tea with <i>one</i> mortal in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 09-16-2021, 09:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T12:13:47-07:00","id":1461586,"title":"","content":"So just to be clear this is a Mage game. But my character has a few antagonists in the Vampire world. We dont have any Vampire players. One of those antagonists is a Ventrue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T17:48:05-07:00","id":1461631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mezlabor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1461586#post1461586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So just to be clear this is a Mage game. But my character has a few antagonists in the Vampire world. We dont have any Vampire players. One of those antagonists is a Ventrue</div> </div> </div> </div>They know what your ST wants them to know, it is impossible to say for sure without knowing your ST. Even because this knowledge may vary a lot between vampires.<br /> <br /> Your best course of action here is to use your abilities to figure it out in game. Your character doesn't have a way to know beforehand, either. It is very rare in the WoD for a faction to know so much about the other as to be sure on what the other knows back, and the Technocracy isn't such a case. Then your character is likely to have the same doubt and want to find out.<br /> <br /> IIRC you have Mind 4. Probe them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T22:37:12-07:00","id":1461796,"title":"","content":"Let's see if I can create an organized, categorized (but not exhaustive) list.<br /> <br /> 1) Historic reasons why Vampires in general might know about the Technocracy:<br /> <br /> - The Tremere and Order of Hermes thing. &quot;My enemy's enemy is my friend.&quot;<br /> <br /> - The need for sleepy ancient Vampires to adapt their Abilities. An ancient Vampire has trained in the use of a spear. He goes into torpor, wakes up a thousand years later with the desire to kill a rival Vampire. He grabs his trusty spear, Obfuscates and explores the world, feeding along the way. He discovers that muskets are the weapon of the day and that all those nights spent mastering the spear are a bit of a waste. He might want to use those Mental Disciplines to investigate who is behind technological changes in the field of war and other areas of life. Imagine he trains at horseback riding (with Animalism) in order to be able to communicate with allies faster than his enemies can. He goes into torpor again and wakes up in the Internet Age. Vampires who become aware of technological change would want to make contact with those responsible in order to receive advice about what to expect in the future.<br /> <br /> - Navigation, Astronomy and Shipbuilding Technology. Vampires connected to European Monarchies would have had a keen interest in the development of science and technology that facilitated travel by ship across oceans. There could easily have been Technocracy Constructs funded by ambitious Vampires.<br /> <br /> 2) Milieus in which Vampires and Technocrats might meet and have common ground:<br /> <br /> - A Toreador architect meets an It-X Macrotechnician architect at a builders' conference. They are both passionate about building-aesthetics and skylines. Each tells the other a little about their Clan/Convention. <br /> <br /> - A Vampire with a Herd becomes interested in the ability of humans to recover from blood loss, replenish and produce more blood. He starts consulting people in the medical community and meets a Progenitor Mage equally interested in studying a willing Vampire test subject.<br /> <br /> - A competitive Lasombra Vampire wants to improve her chess so she can impress others in her Clan. She meets an It-X Statistician at a chess club. He is in the process of developing the most cutting edge chess learning software. She is more than happy to test it out. <br /> <br /> 3) Overlapping interests that more often lead to conflict, mandating information gathering:<br /> <br /> - The Syndicate know how to deal with sleeper investors so that the Convention can steer the global economy in the direction they think is best. A substantial portion of global wealth is held by Vampires who have built their fortunes over centuries. The Syndicate can't easily influence these wealthy Vampires who are playing a longer game than sleepers. Vampires have difficulty maintaining claim over their fortunes due to having outlived their mortal identities. The Ghouls who Vampires use to maintain their fortunes make for easy targets of Magick during the day. <br /> <br /> - When Vampires select humans to become their Progeny, they look for Extraordinary qualities. The Technocracy seeks to bring all Extraordinary Citizens into their fold. <br /> <br /> - NWO's Ivory Tower rewrites history when necessary to shape the Consensus. Vampires who witnessed events being rewritten might object and try to oust the Awakened Academics from their respective universities.<br /> <br /> 4) Circumstances under which Mage Actors would willingly supply information to Vampires about the Technocracy (excluding the subject of Mage Ghouls already discussed at length on the forum):<br /> <br /> - If there is conflict between Vampires and the Technocracy in a given area or field of influence, Tradition Spies can advise Vampires about who they are dealing with, what weaknesses to target.<br /> <br /> - A peace treaty is signed, after some conflict, describing what Technocracy interests Vampires agree to leave alone. A Construct whose location was already discovered (attacked even) by Vampires during the conflict is described in terms of the good work it does for Humanity.<br /> <br /> -","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-27T23:54:20-07:00","id":1461799,"title":"","content":"As one of my players said, &quot;I have a Goth witch friend who says a lot of weird shit. Like the fact they are constantly hunted by evil Star Trek people. Then again, she levitates by eating shrooms.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-28T09:31:21-07:00","id":1461832,"title":"","content":"The reason why vampires are frequently seen as the least informed of the splats is just that as the first splat they were developed without influence of others in their basic cosmology. But there is no reason for them to be well versed in the Union ways. But again, things vary a lot among individuals and depend a lot on the ST view on things instead of any objective fact.<br /> <br /> Auspex can identify Mages at level 2, and is a rather common Discipline. Tremere were a part of the Order of Hermes until the early 13th century, as the Order took decades to expel them even after learning they'd become vampires. Nosferatu are extremely effective information dealers and Obfuscate is just too effective at what it does if you're not expecting it. But above all, Ancillae and Elders play a very long term game.<br /> <br /> Kindred were Illuminatti-like conspirators guiding human society way before Mages thought to do the same. A lot of them have more than 200 years, which predates the Thecnocratic Union itself, many have more than 400, predating the betrayal of the Solificati, and the entire Order of Reason have about 700 years. A long history for Mages, but there are vampires that have been active for longer than that.<br /> <br /> So those creatures are long-lived, organized, and wherever the Union spread its tentacles the vampires were already present. They're actually likely to have ghouls and sleeping agents inside the Union proper, depending on the ST. So it was not a joke, depending on the ST those vampires can go all the way from total ignorant about the Union to be in actual control of your bosses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T00:48:06-07:00","id":1461927,"title":"","content":"Mages and Vampires... don't really share timezones. They don't compete for influence because their goals aren't incompatible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-29T10:59:04-07:00","id":1461979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1461927#post1461927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages and Vampires... don't really share timezones. They don't compete for influence because their goals aren't incompatible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not completely true. As much as their goals aren't incompatible they may be competing for resources and harm one another's plans. Two conspirators influencing the mayor may direct them to irreconcilable actions.<br /> <br /> Also, competition is irrelevant. By diving in some common institutions for their respective purposes they may learn about each other simply as a necessity of the craft. They are, after all, aspects of that institution for the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T02:44:23-07:00","id":1463299,"title":"","content":"I think they are Kindred who know about the Technocracy, but they are a very, very small group (at most a hundred? Maybe a bit more.) But these Vampires do know the Convention names, goals, and outlooks, some of the capabilities (including the fact that Hyperscience is comparable in potential to Mystic Magick), can ascertain levels of influence relative to a situation, are aware that Technocrats are <i>different</i> from mortals, have ways to contact Technocrats etc. This includes some Vampire Princes and Primogen who have vague (yet strangely profitable) deals with the Technomancers.<br /> <br /> Then there are some Kindred (maybe around a thousand, maybe more) who know a bit, who have an inkling. Maybe they talked briefly to some Technocrats or agents, or maybe they tried to ascertain some facts from watching the results of Technocrats' actions. But ultimately they miss in major ways with their comprehension of the Technocracy. Some see it simply as some secret, advanced part of the mortal governments. Others think it is just a conspiracy of old money families who fund secret research in science. Those that have some more information just cannot understand that there the NWO and the Syndicate are wholly separate and different. The variety and potential of Hypertechnology are not known about, and Technocrats are assumed to simply be powerful and influential mortals, rather than Mages. These Kindred do have a distinct impression that there is some <i>other</i> group or faction out there which matters and is capable...but they just lack the information and insight required to ascertain facts correctly.<br /> <br /> In the book <i>Midnight Siege</i> the Giovanni narrator recalls how once the Masquerade got maintained by an outside force despite a Sabbat attack, and that the location of Sabbat headquarters got pointed out to the Camarilla through a reference in the news. Later he encounters an old man on life support in a hotel, who is being wheeled out by mirrorshades agents. The Giovanni Vampire makes brief eye contact and notes that this person is older than anyone who he knows. Probably a Technocrat of the Syndicate or the NWO.<br /> <br /> From time to time Technocrats do make some rather overt actions that might be visible to Kindred. Say a new prosecutor or a judge is brought into a town, and he not only becomes very influential and hard to budge but also seems to be following a clear agenda at times. And has three bodyguards attending him at all times, just in case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-10-2021, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T08:14:40-07:00","id":1463317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1463299#post1463299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then there are some Kindred (maybe around a thousand, maybe more) who know a bit, who have an inkling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that any Kindred with Auspex 2 can see auras and ascertain for sure that a technocrat is a kind of Mage. Giovanni may not find this out because they're the dumb Cappadocians that ditched Auspex, but the Toreador know.<br /> <br /> Also, both the Tremere and the Nosferatu are likely to have extensive databases on the Union. The Nosferatu are also likely to have extensive contact with the VA given how both groups work, while the Tremere have contacts on House Tytalus. Both the VA and OoH are well versed in Technocratic lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T10:21:27-07:00","id":1463325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1463317#post1463317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that any Kindred with Auspex 2 can see auras and ascertain for sure that a technocrat is a kind of Mage. Giovanni may not find this out because they're the dumb Cappadocians that ditched Auspex, but the Toreador know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't the characteristic Aura of a Mage only visible when they are using Magick? I recall an in-universe piece in one of VtM books when the Kindred speaking noted that a Mage's Aura sparkled when he was using luck Spells in a casino.<br /> <br /> Note that Technocrats are subtler than other Mages, and the Technocrats a Kindred is most likely to meet are the ones from the Syndicate (who are specifically noted as having a modicum of respect for Vampires) and the NWO, who are among the most Coincidental Magick users. These might make it harder to glimpse their Aura's telltale Mage characteristics. (let's say 4-5 successes required in game terms, possibly) <br /> (And maybe Auras of Technocrats have different telltale signs than Mystical Mages?)<br /> <br /> Even if a Kindred notes the signs in a Technocrat's Aura, they would have to also be familiar with Mystical Mages to have a point of comparison. And then to derive meaningful facts from the information, they must know who Mages are - that they have Paradigm, Avatars, Essences, various extra abilities...Otherwise, a Kindred would have just a very rough idea that these 'advanced scientists' are somehow different from mortals.<br /> <br /> My point is that it is hard for a Vampire to realize and become fully aware that these are actually <i>Technocrats</i>. Note that the Technocracy does sound pretty unbelievable - the way they push for the development of science with the Time Table, their hidden Constructs around the world (did you know the Progenitors have uplifted octopuses in underwater bases ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), an entire Convention dedicated to space exploration (to put it simply), the Ascension War, influencing the Consensus, etc. And I don't see it happening that a Technocrat would demonstrate or describe (except in most vague and general terms) any of these, or how it exactly works, to a Kindred. Maybe these are some exceptions - like I wrote, maybe very, very few Kindred actually <i>know </i>about the Technocracy. It takes a lot of information gathering and confirmations to get to the truth about the Technomancers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1463317#post1463317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, both the Tremere and the Nosferatu are likely to have extensive databases on the Union. The Nosferatu are also likely to have extensive contact with the VA given how both groups work, while the Tremere have contacts on House Tytalus. Both the VA and OoH are well versed in Technocratic lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere probably have knowledge about the Technocracy available within their Clan. I see them as staying totally up to date in regard to any development with Mages - through full knowledge about the existence of the Order of Hermes they must know about the Traditions, as they simply would not ignore being knowledgable about such an important group. And from being familiar with Traditions, sooner or later they would find out about the Technocracy. Or it could happen separately, of course.<br /> <br /> Some Nosferatu probably do know, but I'd say not that many. And do note that there is the possibility for misinformation and misconceptions to be introduced - it just might be the work of the NWO that some Nosferatu are convinced that there are only three Conventions or that Technocracy has far less influence and resources than it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-10-2021, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-10T19:18:12-07:00","id":1463362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1463325#post1463325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It takes a lot of information gathering and confirmations to get to the truth about the Technomancers.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said earlier in the thread, there are several possible ways to work this out.<br /> <br /> By Vampire RAW there is no difference in the aura regarding Paradigm, so all the subtlety means nothing. You can add it yourself? Sure. But you can't say this is the only correct approach. The V20 table is unclear if a Mage is detected only when performing or not (previous editions were more clear on detecting Mages regardless of conjuration), but again it doesn't mean one answer is more likely than the other, it is up to ST interpretation. Finally it isn't clear if the sparkles count as shade, color or pattern, so it can take between 1 and 3 successes. Finally it doesn't differentiate Mage, Sorcerer or Magic Merit user.<br /> <br /> You can, by RAW, decide that it needs to be 3 successes and only during casting, that even then it is completely impossible to distinguish the kind of magic user, and you will be keeping with the spirit of the rules if you decide that subtle technomancers take far more to even perceive as something strange. But a ST can also decide that 1 success is enough to detect any magic user and 2 or 3 are enough to identify types. Not to mention how much information a vampire with 3 or more in Auspex can glare.<br /> <br /> Now, what will the Kindred learn from this tidbit of information? At most I think the number of vampires that heard rumors about those sciency types with weird auras would be greater than just 1k world-wide, but otherwise your take on the subject is pretty valid. It just isn't necessarily the only valid or interesting one, or keeping to the opening post, the one to expect from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26766\" data-vbnamecard=\"26766\">mezlabor</a>'s ST. How can I know?<br /> <br /> Clan Nosferatu keep the shrecknet, so I wouldn't dismiss their information so readily. They are professional information brokers and tightly united as a clan on this front, and their databases are digital, so not hard for <i>them</i> to access. Shrecknet was already canonically praised by the Virtual Adepts as a mysterious network they couldn't yet hack into, so it isn't something to be brushed aside.<br /> <br /> What I'm getting at is that even with full consideration for the lore across every line, this is far from settled. The books keep from entering too much crossover territory on purpose, so the amount of knowledge and relationships between splats is completely up to interpretation. And in this thread's context we can only try to guess what will be mezlabor's ST take on this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":5826,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","user":"monteparnas","date":".  code bug 10-20-2021, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T00:49:12-07:00","id":1464475,"title":"","content":"So to answer this because its been awhile since we posted. The answer for our chronicle is they didnt know much. After some bad tabloids got seeded about a stalker stalking my pop star (the toreador) and a campaign on social media to cancel the ventrues business interests we eventually had a sit down with the ventrue. They didnt know who we were exactly only that we were part of a powerful global conspiracy of business peoples and scientists that were connected to magik. He was quite impressed actually. We hammered out an agreement that was mutually beneficial and he made my toreador problem dissapear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26766-mezlabor","name":"mezlabor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T02:06:21-07:00","id":1464481,"title":"","content":"Vampires are hilariously mostly kind of the low level mooks of the setting.<br /> <br /> A vampire Elder controls a multi-billion dollar corporation that wields influence internationally.<br /> <br /> A Syndicate Comptroller controls the value of currency and the concept of economics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T18:20:06-07:00","id":1464672,"title":"","content":"I disagree, but I don't think this is a very productive line of debate for now, at least while I still have a light headache from my problem with the PC earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T09:53:46-07:00","id":1464882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464481#post1464481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are hilariously mostly kind of the low level mooks of the setting.<br /> <br /> A vampire Elder controls a multi-billion dollar corporation that wields influence internationally.<br /> <br /> A Syndicate Comptroller controls the value of currency and the concept of economics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like what an arrogant Mage would try to sell to a Kindred. &quot;Guardians of reality&quot;, &quot;Followers of Ascension&quot;, &quot;Safekeepers of deepest secrets&quot; and all that...<br /> Mages have to deal with carrying their Foci, following their Paradigm, preparing and casting Effects, Paradox, and being relatively fragile. While the abilities of the Kindred are more innate and can be used at a moment's notice. Ghouling and blood bonding are immensely useful. As is the ability to embrace, of course. Also I think the basic potency of Disciplines is greater than that of Magick, barring long and arduous rituals or specific Rotes.<br /> <br /> I recall from one of MtA books that Technocrats should always wear mirroshades in encounters with Vampires, or they will &quot;become a casualty&quot;.<br /> In <i>Coteries of New York</i> Sophie Langley constantly (or at least very often) has Presence-derived charisma around her, and it is strong enough to keep the PC in line and also to instantly tell a Second Inquisition team to be gone from the PC's Haven (not certain if it's SI, might be just regular police sent by another Kindred). And her Majesty is effective enough to make eight SI strike force members stop in tracks while they are killed one by one by a Brujah and her. I just do not see Mages having such sheer potency of Effects without needing very specific circumstances or performing long rituals (and this has to be hanged with Time 4).<br /> <br /> Sure a Vampire Neonate is in trouble if he messes with a couple of Mages of Arete 3-4 or a Master Mage. But if we're talking about a Vampire Neonate, then maybe she or he should be compared to Arete 1-2 Mages. And such Mages, well...one certainty they have is that they can run back to their Chantry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Or try to stall for time by showing some nice Magick. Changing colors of items with Matter, influencing card draws or dice rolls with Entropy...might just make a Kindred consider a Mage differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-22-2021, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T10:31:33-07:00","id":1464886,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting that CTPhipps said &quot;mostly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Among the three &quot;main&quot; splats, Mages probably start off with the lowest &quot;power level,&quot; but end up with the highest, generally.<br /> <br /> Werewolves start with the highest &quot;power level,&quot; but have the least potential of the three, aside from the &quot;Bigger Fish&quot; in the Umbra that they can collaborate with when needed.<br /> <br /> Vampires start off in the middle between Mages and Werewolves, but rival Mages for the highest potential of the three major splats. But that's partially because the actual top limits of vampiric power have always been left purely in Storyteller fiat territory, whereas hard rules for the upper limits of True Magic's power have been put down once or twice. Go check out the thread in Mage about building to fight an Ante if you want to dig into that more.<br /> <br /> <br /> But it is probably fair to say that Vampires are the least-informed splat about the wider World of Darkness, simply by virtue of how little involvement they have with the various Umbra, where is where a lot of the rest of the World of Darkness operates pretty regularly. Add on that most of what the Technocracy is doing out in the open is going to be very Coincidental, and it is going to be the rare vampire that even picks up traces of what the Union is up to.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, there are going to be vampires that are, to varying extents, in the know, because there are going to be the rare days where a Union member is caught without their mirrorshades, and then they get milked for information with Dominate, Presence, and Auspex. Even then, the fact that members of the Union tend to operate on a need-to-know basis means that few prisoners will be able to give up much more than a single cell or organization, one piece of the network. The number of vampires that get their hands on someone with broad knowledge of the Union's operations, or continuing putting the whole thing together one lead at a time over many years, are going to be very small. And the general trend among vampires is to keep knowledge like that as a private advantage rather than share it publicly, in my opinion. The only reason I could see that changing was if they perceived the Union as an existential threat, where rallying every vampire against it was necessary for survival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T10:32:46-07:00","id":1464887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464481#post1464481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Syndicate Comptroller controls the value of currency and the concept of economics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they don't. If they did there would be no Ascension War.<br /> <br /> I'd say vampires have generally far more deep and fine influence over infiltrated institutions than Mages do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T10:47:03-07:00","id":1464888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464886#post1464886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth noting that CTPhipps said &quot;mostly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Among the three &quot;main&quot; splats, Mages probably start off with the lowest &quot;power level,&quot; but end up with the highest, generally.<br /> <br /> Werewolves start with the highest &quot;power level,&quot; but have the least potential of the three, aside from the &quot;Bigger Fish&quot; in the Umbra that they can collaborate with when needed.<br /> <br /> Vampires start off in the middle between Mages and Werewolves, but rival Mages for the highest potential of the three major splats. But that's partially because the actual top limits of vampiric power have always been left purely in Storyteller fiat territory, whereas hard rules for the upper limits of True Magic's power have been put down once or twice. Go check out the thread in Mage about building to fight an Ante if you want to dig into that more.<br /> <br /> <br /> But it is probably fair to say that Vampires are the least-informed splat about the wider World of Darkness, simply by virtue of how little involvement they have with the various Umbra, where is where a lot of the rest of the World of Darkness operates pretty regularly. Add on that most of what the Technocracy is doing out in the open is going to be very Coincidental, and it is going to be the rare vampire that even picks up traces of what the Union is up to.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, there are going to be vampires that are, to varying extents, in the know, because there are going to be the rare days where a Union member is caught without their mirrorshades, and then they get milked for information with Dominate, Presence, and Auspex. Even then, the fact that members of the Union tend to operate on a need-to-know basis means that few prisoners will be able to give up much more than a single cell or organization, one piece of the network. The number of vampires that get their hands on someone with broad knowledge of the Union's operations, or continuing putting the whole thing together one lead at a time over many years, are going to be very small. And the general trend among vampires is to keep knowledge like that as a private advantage rather than share it publicly, in my opinion. The only reason I could see that changing was if they perceived the Union as an existential threat, where rallying every vampire against it was necessary for survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>One problem here is that Astral Travel never got to be defined. Are Vampires that cut out of the Umbra, or did the game just silent on the matter because it shouldn't matter?<br /> <br /> But more important for the Union side, they may not perceive magic, but they'll perceive two things that Kindred pay a lot of attention to: manipulation and power. An organization of this kind and reach is bound to get attention from control freaks that cultivate influence for centuries. And is likely to have some moles inside already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T10:56:47-07:00","id":1464889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464888#post1464888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem here is that Astral Travel never got to be defined. Are Vampires that cut out of the Umbra, or did the game just silent on the matter because it shouldn't matter?<br /> <br /> But more important for the Union side, they may not perceive magic, but they'll perceive two things that Kindred pay a lot of attention to: manipulation and power. An organization of this kind and reach is bound to get attention from control freaks that cultivate influence for centuries. And is likely to have some moles inside already.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said &quot;little involvement,&quot; not &quot;cut off,&quot; for a reason. I wasn't thinking too much about Auspex admittedly, but we are talking about the fifth level of the Discipline. Level 5 Auspex and Blood Magic like Spirit Manipulation are precisely what I am thinking of when I say &quot;little involvement.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I agree, there are going to be plenty of vampires that have infiltrated some components of the Technocracy. But given that the majority of those working for the Technocracy know little to nothing about the &quot;big picture,&quot; the majority of vampires with infiltrators are similarly going to have limited knowledge of the &quot;big picture.&quot; They'll know that there's some economic or political conspiracy, or some super-tech laboratory, but few vampires below the level of Methuselah are going to be able to connect the dots and actually see The Technocratic Union, in no small part because few vampires below that level will be equipped to follow the trail of breadcrumbs when it dips into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> P.S. While I haven't looked into it too much to know the details, I should probably include Technomancy Paths as another potentially viable route of uncovering real dirt on the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Also, my personal preference for Auspex 5 is that you start in the Periphery, with the potential to move into the Astral Penumbra and beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 10-22-2021, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T11:38:42-07:00","id":1464894,"title":"","content":"Adding time to the equation, I'd say it is more than just Methuselah, but it surely don't have to be in any way common knowledge. But I do think it can be more common than most people assume, because a big part of the impression on Kindred ignorance have to do only with how the books are written.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking they all avoid telling much about other lines, but most splats have their Theories of Everything that kind of give the impression that they're more 'in the know' even when they actually aren't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T12:26:41-07:00","id":1464895,"title":"","content":"Lower ranks, nothing unless it\u2019s a special case (invested in appropriate Lore).<br /> <br /> Upper ranks of Camarilla: there\u2019s a group of technowizards (who don\u2019t like being called that) who work to maintain the masquerade on their own part. We have an understanding where they leave policing the Kindred to us as long as we maintain the masquerade, but they\u2019ll occasionally take out a flagrant vampire outside our territory that isn\u2019t being policed.<br /> <br /> Upper ranks of the Sabbat: some hunters who take out Cainites who flaunt the masquerade have advanced tech we\u2019ve never seen. The Tremere in our ranks think they might be wizards or at least supplied by them, but we have few survivors of encounters to provide confirmation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 10-23-2021, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T12:58:33-07:00","id":1464898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464888#post1464888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One problem here is that Astral Travel never got to be defined. Are Vampires that cut out of the Umbra, or did the game just silent on the matter because it shouldn't matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>This has always been a major weakness of Vampire. I kept anticipating that in some future sourcebook - a Players Guide, an Storyteller Handbook, a Thaumaturgy supplement, etc. - would provide STs more details on how vampires utilize Auspex 5. What do they find there? What kind of adventures or events could happen? What other kinds of astral projectors would they meet? How can it be used as storytelling device, not just a gimmick to spy on someone in the physical world?<br /> <br /> I imagine many players would just use the power to occasionally spy on other vampires or mortals and didn't need anything more. But there had to be other players than me that wanted to use the power to do more with it. Or STs that wanted to spice things up for players with that power. But we never got any guidance for it, so any ST interested would have to figure things out for themselves. Sure, we did have sourcebooks in other games, like the Book of Worlds for Mage, that addressed the astral, but nothing targeted for the needs of Vampire PCs which was what was needed. So it was going to take a lot of work. I always thought there should have been a 5 page or so section in the VtM Storytellers Handbook that addressed this. Its lack thereof in second edition is to be expected - other gamelines would be more concerned with the Astral, like Mage. But by Revised once the basics had been established, a new edition should have developed it for use in Vampire.<br /> <br /> I've compiled over a dozen pages of notes I took from the Book of Worlds, what I liked in horror or fantasy stories that involved the astral plane, and some non-fiction reading done on it as an occult/magic phenomenon. So I think I'm somewhat prepared to actually ST a PC through the Astral. However, ever since I created these notes I've never run a game with a player whose PC ever learned Auspex 5 so I've never seen how it turned out in actual play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T13:03:48-07:00","id":1464899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464887#post1464887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except they don't. If they did there would be no Ascension War.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, the Technocracy holds an impenetrable rock solid hold on the Consensus pre-Avatar Storm. When the Technocracy identifies a mage, if they're feeling hostile, then your family turns on you because the police know you to be a pedophile, your bank account vanishes, you find a clone in your place if they get a sample of your hair brush, and otherwise the entire world is suddeny against you.<br /> <br /> It's like the Matrix, the Technocracy is totally on the offensive and the Traditions are forced to hide in Narnia because they control the economy, government, ABC agencies, and media.<br /> <br /> I mean, the only reason the Union lost was because literally a tidal wave of the Damned ATE 80% of all mages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464882#post1464882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like what an arrogant Mage would try to sell to a Kindred. &quot;Guardians of reality&quot;, &quot;Followers of Ascension&quot;, &quot;Safekeepers of deepest secrets&quot; and all that...<br /> Mages have to deal with carrying their Foci, following their Paradigm, preparing and casting Effects, Paradox, and being relatively fragile. While the abilities of the Kindred are more innate and can be used at a moment's notice. Ghouling and blood bonding are immensely useful. As is the ability to embrace, of course. Also I think the basic potency of Disciplines is greater than that of Magick, barring long and arduous rituals or specific Rotes.<br /> <br /> I recall from one of MtA books that Technocrats should always wear mirroshades in encounters with Vampires, or they will &quot;become a casualty&quot;.<br /> In <i>Coteries of New York</i> Sophie Langley constantly (or at least very often) has Presence-derived charisma around her, and it is strong enough to keep the PC in line and also to instantly tell a Second Inquisition team to be gone from the PC's Haven (not certain if it's SI, might be just regular police sent by another Kindred). And her Majesty is effective enough to make eight SI strike force members stop in tracks while they are killed one by one by a Brujah and her. I just do not see Mages having such sheer potency of Effects without needing very specific circumstances or performing long rituals (and this has to be hanged with Time 4).<br /> <br /> Sure a Vampire Neonate is in trouble if he messes with a couple of Mages of Arete 3-4 or a Master Mage. But if we're talking about a Vampire Neonate, then maybe she or he should be compared to Arete 1-2 Mages. And such Mages, well...one certainty they have is that they can run back to their Chantry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Or try to stall for time by showing some nice Magick. Changing colors of items with Matter, influencing card draws or dice rolls with Entropy...might just make a Kindred consider a Mage differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit this is a preference but this reminds me of, &quot;Who would win, a Garou or vampire?&quot; and my response is, &quot;What self-respecting vampire would EVER go after a Garou personally?&quot; In my games, when Garou and Vampires fight, the former win every time in physical confrontations (because it's usually 4-1 anyway) but Vampires DON'T fight in physical confrontations. They fight with police, drive-by ghouls, car bombs, going after kinfolk, and other influence,<br /> <br /> Yes, a vampire can break a mage's neck if he's face to face with them.<br /> <br /> However, if you let a vampire get face to face with you, you're a pretty poor Technocrat. Same with being a vampire elder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-22-2021, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T13:09:47-07:00","id":1464901,"title":"","content":"There is plenty of evidence that, however powerful the Technocracy is, their hold on Reality is not rock-solid. Pentex infiltration via Syndicate affiliations was a thing long before the Avatar Storm, and the Financial Crisis of the late 2000s wouldn't have been a thing if the Syndicate had complete control over the economy. They may be the best in the field, but they aren't the only thing that matters.<br /> <br /> The fact that vicious blood-sucking brain-washing immortals don't rank as a priority on the Technocracy's to-do list is actually pretty good evidence that they don't have the whole world in the palm of their hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 10-22-2021, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T14:03:57-07:00","id":1464909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464901#post1464901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is plenty of evidence that, however powerful the Technocracy is, their hold on Reality is not rock-solid. Pentex infiltration via Syndicate affiliations was a thing long before the Avatar Storm, and the Financial Crisis of the late 2000s wouldn't have been a thing if the Syndicate had complete control over the economy. They may be the best in the field, but they aren't the only thing that matters.<br /> <br /> The fact that vicious blood-sucking brain-washing immortals don't rank as a priority on the Technocracy's to-do list is actually pretty good evidence that they don't have the whole world in the palm of their hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that with an asterisk that the Technocracy has a rock solid hold on reality in terms of Paradigm but have failed to achieve their end results because of Nephandi/Pentex/Human Fraily corruption of their ideals. Which is to say that everyone believes in their Paradigm (anti-vaxxers aside) but this hasn't achieved Ascension or enlightenment but become another tool for human greed and exploitation.<br /> <br /> Which is to say they wanted to build Star Trek's Federation and they've gotten stuck in Cyberpunk 2020 somehow.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy, of course, blames the Traditions for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T14:59:55-07:00","id":1464914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464481#post1464481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are hilariously mostly kind of the low level mooks of the setting.<br /> <br /> A vampire Elder controls a multi-billion dollar corporation that wields influence internationally.<br /> <br /> A Syndicate Comptroller controls the value of currency and the concept of economics.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of the Comptroller controlling the concept of economics, I would make a comparison with an old theological question (in two parts):<br /> <br /> 1. Can God make an object that is totally indestructible? - if yes,<br /> 2. Now that the object exists, can God destroy the indestructible thing?<br /> <br /> The Syndicate boss, say one who has lived through much of history since the industrial revolution, worked with a bunch of other Mages to insert the concept of economics into the Consensus. It has had time to solidify, in a metaphysical sense. He may wish to adjust it according to current-day strategic needs, but would need to do some serious Magick and mundane propaganda to make said adjustment.<br /> <br /> I agree with the general idea that Vampires playing the market do so on a playground that the Syndicate controls. Elder Vampires with Mage-Lore would be fully conscious of the Syndicate's power and would likely attempt to restrain younger Vampires from engaging in street level conflict with any kind of Mage, to avoid having their fortunes stripped away during daylight hours.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464882#post1464882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure a Vampire Neonate is in trouble if he messes with a couple of Mages of Arete 3-4 or a Master Mage. But if we're talking about a Vampire Neonate, then maybe she or he should be compared to Arete 1-2 Mages. And such Mages, well...one certainty they have is that they can run back to their Chantry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Or try to stall for time by showing some nice Magick. Changing colors of items with Matter, influencing card draws or dice rolls with Entropy...might just make a Kindred consider a Mage differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>At first thought, I would think it cruel to limit players to Arete 1 or 2 in a setting with roving bands of Vampires. However, consider what that leaves the player to purchase with unspent freebies. At Arete 1, the player has 15 freebie points to spend on Willpower, Merits and additional Backgrounds on top of the 7 already allowed. Arcane 5 is easily affordable, making the character almost undetectable. I think this kind of limitation on Magickal ability in the face of predacious undead would just force players to craft Hunters rather than characters pursuing enlightenment, since survival is such an immediate priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 10-22-2021, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:09:26-07:00","id":1464917,"title":"","content":"As an ST explained it to me in the 90s.<br /> <br /> &quot;A vampire with Lure of the Flames 5 can burn a building to the ground and incinerate everything around him if he's willing to die in the resulting fire.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A mage with Forces 5 can destroy a city if he's willing to die in the resulting Paradox Backlash.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:40:11-07:00","id":1464923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464917#post1464917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an ST explained it to me in the 90s.<br /> <br /> &quot;A vampire with Lure of the Flames 5 can burn a building to the ground and incinerate everything around him if he's willing to die in the resulting fire.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A mage with Forces 5 can destroy a city if he's willing to die in the resulting Paradox Backlash.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou and Fera with fire-resisting Gifts: &quot;What the hell happened here?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T17:01:31-07:00","id":1464938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464923#post1464923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou and Fera with fire-resisting Gifts: &quot;What the hell happened here?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why Marauders and Taftani are so terrifying.<br /> <br /> It's actually a testament to the self-control of mages that powerful that WMD events don't happen more often.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T21:31:37-07:00","id":1464962,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy don't control the Consensus and never did. Winning the war for the Consensus is about slowly shaping it, not outright controlling it. A vampire manipulating the market is playing in a field the Syndicate nurtured and shaped, but is otherwise as independent from them as a garden is from the gardener. Actually, as a city park is from the public officials that planned it.<br /> <br /> Mages work top down and vampires bottom up. Those are completely different approaches to manipulation with pros and cons. And the Jyhad is as global and encompassing as the Ascension War, with the added aspect of being far older. The Union in its current form is younger than some Ancilla, and the Order of Reason is younger than many Elders.<br /> <br /> And nothing here is about supernatural power. We're talking influence and information, and for both groups their magical powers are just a tool in this regard. A bit of preternatural control over an asset here and there works wonders, but doesn't make a winner.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk power, though, make at least a sensible comparison. You know what else differentiate Lure of Flames 5 from Forces 5? The former is available for a starting character if you want, while the later takes enough time, effort and XP to build up that the Vampire PC could very well have a level 6 or 7 Discipline by then.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, I think you're the only one here that prefer 1st edition Technocracy. That's not a problem, but isn't conducive of a good discussion either when we're just not talking about the same thing. This thread in particular is about Revised Technocracy, as OP is in a game of Technocracy PCs using Revised and GttT and asking from this POV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T21:34:46-07:00","id":1464964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464962#post1464962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a>, I think you're the only one here that prefer 1st edition Technocracy. That's not a problem, but isn't conducive of a good discussion either when we're just not talking about the same thing. This thread in particular is about Revised Technocracy, as OP is in a game of Technocracy PCs using Revised and GttT and asking from this POV.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironic fact, I don't play Traditions games. I only play Union and the occasional Hollow One. That's because the absolute best way to play the Technocratic Union is &quot;boots on the ground&quot; with the fact your superiors are evil and you can't trust them. To get that full <i>La Femme Nikita</i> and <i>X-files </i>thing where you are doing your best to do the moral thing while your superiors only care about results.<br /> <br /> That's why I don't like softening the Technocracy because it removes a lot of what makes roleplaying a member fun.<br /> <br /> But even in the &quot;reformed&quot; Technocracy, the Union wields vast-vast power and still will be able to crush any vampire, IMHO. The thing that separates vampires and mages? Mages WORK TOGETHER.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T04:16:53-07:00","id":1464995,"title":"","content":"<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464898#post1464898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has always been a major weakness of Vampire. I kept anticipating that in some future sourcebook - a Players Guide, an Storyteller Handbook, a Thaumaturgy supplement, etc. - would provide STs more details on how vampires utilize Auspex 5. What do they find there? What kind of adventures or events could happen? What other kinds of astral projectors would they meet? How can it be used as storytelling device, not just a gimmick to spy on someone in the physical world?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I have been wondering about the specifics and opportunities of Astral Travel of Kindred as well. Travelling 1000 miles per hour sounds pretty amazing, as is being able to use Auspex while in Astral Form. I've been thinking about many particulars in regards to Vampires travelling on the Astral Plane. How often do Kindred meet each other on the Astral Plane, and is there some general non-hostility followed (gotta respect fellow astral traveller after all, and better not risk fighting in such an unkown area) ? Which Clans are the most active in it, and do they form groups / Coteries that meet up on the Astral Plane and explore it? When fighting occurs, can Kindred do this awesome thing that they conjure weapons as manifestations of their will? So even non-combatant Toreador or Tremere flash out swords and daggers if it gets serious. Or Tremere could be fighting in astral combat with manifestations inspired by occult concepts. Finally - just what is there to do on the Astral Plane for a Kindred, and how many Kindred seek mysteries and wonders of it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464917#post1464917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an ST explained it to me in the 90s.<br /> <br /> &quot;A vampire with Lure of the Flames 5 can burn a building to the ground and incinerate everything around him if he's willing to die in the resulting fire.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;A mage with Forces 5 can destroy a city if he's willing to die in the resulting Paradox Backlash.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This one doesn't make sense to me. Why would the difficulty of a Magick Effect that is drawn from the number of disbelieving witnesses be as simple as a binary &quot;There are some / there aren't any&quot;? It makes sense that the more witnesses there are, the harder an Effect is to pull off. Maybe not to the point of there being a difference between 5, 10, or 60 mundane humans being nearby...but certainly a thousand, ten thousand or hundred thousand mundane humans do create a substantial weight of disbelief. So any attempt at such Magick should fizzle out.<br /> <br /> Forces 5 can probably be used to set a rather large wilderness area on fire, or to devastate an area with a tornado. In such cases it can be Coincidental, and there are usually very few witnesses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464899#post1464899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uh, the Technocracy holds an impenetrable rock solid hold on the Consensus pre-Avatar Storm. When the Technocracy identifies a mage, if they're feeling hostile, then your family turns on you because the police know you to be a pedophile, your bank account vanishes, you find a clone in your place if they get a sample of your hair brush, and otherwise the entire world is suddeny against you.<br /> <br /> It's like the Matrix, the Technocracy is totally on the offensive and the Traditions are forced to hide in Narnia because they control the economy, government, ABC agencies, and media.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 1st edition Technocracy... &quot;<i>The Syndicate is mainly responsible for enforcing the Pogrom against earthbound mages of lesser power. The Syndicate seems to take great delight in systematically destroying every aspect of a mage's life. First it will ruin the mage financially, impugning credit, making bank accounts dissapear, etc. Then it will proceed to frame the mage, destroying his reputation among all he holds dear. Finally, the killing begin, starting with the mage's most distant friends, then relatives, then the mage himself. The Syndicate delights in destroying a person even before it ends his life.</i>&quot; There is very little positive about the Technocracy in this write-up, though there is this cool part about the Syndicate leadership remaining a mystery even for other Technocrats.<br /> <br /> It is actually worse than the Matrix, because in the Matrix the agents are rather simple, and there is the phone booth to run back to. While the Technocrats have so many means...<br /> According to much of what is written in MtA books, the Traditions basically have to hide in their Chantries for most of the time, because Technocrats simply have the edge over them in various ways.<br /> Though if the Technocracy is so powerful, then how it is that the Nephandi still exist and are able to function as the third Mage faction? Kind of an inconsistency here. Assuming the Technocracy effectively won a victory over the Tradtions (in more than one area - influence, military capability, organization...), then why cannot they do so against the less numerous Nephandi?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464914#post1464914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At first thought, I would think it cruel to limit players to Arete 1 or 2 in a setting with roving bands of Vampires. However, consider what that leaves the player to purchase with unspent freebies. At Arete 1, the player has 15 freebie points to spend on Willpower, Merits and additional Backgrounds on top of the 7 already allowed. Arcane 5 is easily affordable, making the character almost undetectable. I think this kind of limitation on Magickal ability in the face of predacious undead would just force players to craft Hunters rather than characters pursuing enlightenment, since survival is such an immediate priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we are talking about Arcane, then a rating of 5 is problematic - it makes it hard to interact with other persons, and for the Mage to have mundane matters within society and institutions. Arcane 2-3 would probably be enough for a considerable degree of safety.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464962#post1464962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages work top down and vampires bottom up. Those are completely different approaches to manipulation with pros and cons. And the Jyhad is as global and encompassing as the Ascension War, with the added aspect of being far older. The Union in its current form is younger than some Ancilla, and the Order of Reason is younger than many Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very good point - the Kindred have the wealth of experience and knowledge that is not visible in Traits or rules, but certainly it matters greatly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-23-2021, 07:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T08:29:58-07:00","id":1465013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464995#post1464995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are talking about Arcane, then a rating of 5 is problematic - it makes it hard to interact with other persons, and for the Mage to have mundane matters within society and institutions. Arcane 2-3 would probably be enough for a considerable degree of safety.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could have influence over people with Arcane 5. Just stand directly in front of someone and tell them what to do. It becomes a subliminal message. You can walk into the mayor's office and install yourself there, with everyone wondering why the coffee pot goes so fast. <br /> <br /> That such a high rating is problematic for social interaction illustrates my point. By limiting a Mage's ability to actually be a Mage and then having them face the prospect of encounters with Vampires, you make the player so prioritize surviving such encounters that they sacrifice roleplaying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T12:49:24-07:00","id":1465029,"title":"","content":"This reasoning sounds like a starting Mage should expect random combat encounters with Vampires. And even then I'm not sure a Mage with Arete 1 is so desperately vulnerable or that it is a problem. The best way to survive a fight is not fighting, I don't know why it isn't an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T13:38:34-07:00","id":1465034,"title":"","content":"Random combat with vampires is actually pretty easily avoided just by taking care of most of your business by day, then hunkering down at night. But random encounters with vampires should most definitely be the exception, not the rule, and it's not any more of an unreasonable threat than potentially having to deal with spirits without having access to the Spirit Sphere. Low-level Mages are going to have encounters they just aren't prepared to handle if they are jumped out in the open. They need to work around that, in one way or another. Which is why Cabals and Amalgams are common, especially among the inexperienced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T19:20:27-07:00","id":1465084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465029#post1465029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThis reasoning sounds like a starting Mage should expect random combat encounters with Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the storyteller says Vampires are part of the setting, players can expect to encounter them. The way Vampires behave, like always trying to blood-bond Mages, players can either expect to fight or be enslaved (which Mages with respectable Arete and Spheres virtually never attempt to do to Vampires despite all kinds of ways they can accomplish that).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465029#post1465029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And even then I'm not sure a Mage with Arete 1 is so desperately vulnerable or that it is a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>If one or more of the Vampires has Celerity, how do the Mages escape? Had they Arete 3+, they could use Correspondence 3 to teleport to safety or Time 3 to run really fast, but were talking Arete 1. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465029#post1465029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best way to survive a fight is not fighting, I don't know why it isn't an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you play a more reasonable Vampire (If I remember correctly, it's your favorite splat to play). If you were a Mage with Arete 1 and 6 sensory abilities, how would you avoid fighting if the Vampires are determined to blood-bond or kill the Cabal? Those with Presence/Dominate can keep trying to capture everyone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465034#post1465034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random combat with vampires is actually pretty easily avoided just by taking care of most of your business by day, then hunkering down at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>What time does a Cult of Ecstasy Mage go out to party? A Hollow One? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465034#post1465034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But random encounters with vampires should most definitely be the exception, not the rule,</div> </div> </div> </div>For sure, I agree. We are talking about a world in which both Mages and Vampires exist. The latter can reproduce at will, so their numbers are determined by their whims. Suppose you are a player who has just joined a troupe and you don't know the storyteller. How often do you expect to encounter Vampires?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465034#post1465034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it's not any more of an unreasonable threat than potentially having to deal with spirits without having access to the Spirit Sphere.</div> </div> </div> </div>... which you would need rank 2 to even affect the Spirit - Arete 1. Yes, almost anything Arete 1 &quot;Mages&quot; encounter is going to steamroll them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465034#post1465034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Low-level Mages are going to have encounters they just aren't prepared to handle if they are jumped out in the open. They need to work around that, in one way or another. Which is why Cabals and Amalgams are common, especially among the inexperienced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am talking abut a Cabal or Amalgam encountering a Coterie or Pack. <br /> <br /> If the storyteller is reasonable and the Vampires are not the standard egomaniacs trying to enslave everyone, the Arete 1 Mages can live to fight another <i>day.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T22:48:34-07:00","id":1465098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465084#post1465084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What time does a Cult of Ecstasy Mage go out to party? A Hollow One?</div> </div> </div> </div>Before dark if they're smart, if you're going to propose a non-standard setting where Mages are artificially weakened and Vampires are unusually aggressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465084#post1465084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For sure, I agree. We are talking about a world in which both Mages and Vampires exist. The latter can reproduce at will, so their numbers are determined by their whims. Suppose you are a player who has just joined a troupe and you don't know the storyteller. How often do you expect to encounter Vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires can reproduce &quot;at will&quot; in theory, but there are plenty of practical limitations to consider, so saying their numbers are determined on a &quot;whim&quot; is unreasonable. Even if you have a Sabbat Pack creating a bunch of shovelheads to toss at the Mages, that's going to take a LOT of work to set up properly, where the deranged neonates get rolling in the right direction at the right opportunity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465084#post1465084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... which you would need rank 2 to even affect the Spirit - Arete 1. Yes, almost anything Arete 1 &quot;Mages&quot; encounter is going to steamroll them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize this is probably where there has been something of a misunderstanding. You had initially posed this hypothetical scenario of Arete-1-only Mages-in-a-Vampire-gangland back on the previous page. I wasn't really thinking of that specifically when responding, but more the general idea of roving gangs of Vampires being a threat that a Mage would typically have to consider. Under the conditions imposed, I'm inclined to agree that the deck is stacked against the Mages in a straight-up conflict; it was just a page or so back that I made a little &quot;tier list&quot; that had beginner Mages come out behind beginner Vampires, especially if you're imposing restrictions on the power level of the Mages without any restrictions on the Vampires. It's trivially true, as is the follow-up that building Mage characters to survive in such a world would require some radically different considerations.<br /> <br /> But I would also mention the caveat that the deck is stacked against the Vampires in one particular regard: detection. Only a minority of beginner-level Vampires will possess Auspex, which is the only way a Vampire can recognize the difference between a Mage and a Sleeper unless they witness them using magic. And I think it was just a page or so back in this thread that it was being debated how effective that method is. In comparison, I can think of ways for nearly half of the level 1 Spheres to pick a Vampire out of a crowd; Life, Entropy, and Prime are pretty obvious, plus Time if you have a Vampire much older than its physical appearance would indicate, and Forces could likely detect their body being at room temperature, etc., etc. Limiting the Mages to only their sensory abilities and then precluding them any chance to use those abilities to avoid the conflict in the first place unbalances the whole thing significantly.<br /> <br /> And in a world where marauding bands of enslaving Vampires are a feature, your Mages should be trained in a radically different skill-set if they expect to survive. They're going to know how to fight without relying too much on their magic, and they're going to be aware of ways to exploit vampiric weaknesses. If they didn't, then they would be dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465084#post1465084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am talking abut a Cabal or Amalgam encountering a Coterie or Pack.<br /> <br /> If the storyteller is reasonable and the Vampires are not the standard egomaniacs trying to enslave everyone, the Arete 1 Mages can live to fight another <i>day.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Reading this a bit more closely, I think this part, along with this part<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465084#post1465084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way Vampires behave, like always trying to blood-bond Mages, players can either expect to fight or be enslaved (which Mages with respectable Arete and Spheres virtually never attempt to do to Vampires despite all kinds of ways they can accomplish that).</div> </div> </div> </div>is the point really needs to be discussed. That's just not the way typical Vampire/Mage crossover goes. Have you ever read the long screed about &quot;turning Vampires into lawn-chairs&quot; that was included in M20? It's been a while, but the big point that it hits on is that it's a very dumb idea for a lot of reasons unless the deck is already ridiculously stacked in your favour. Average Vampires habitually trying to blood-bond Mages is basically the reverse-lawnchair. Getting past the point I made about only a minority of Vampires being equipped to actively seek out Mages, it's the sort of thing that is only rarely going to happen because there will likely be horrible consequences for doing so; the potential of a vengeful master, of colleagues retaliating collectively to discourage precisely that kind of behaviour. If a Vampire is trying to blood-bond your Mage in a normal game of MtAs, you're not going to be dealing with a coterie of neonates, it's going to be an Elder or a Methuselah, 19 times out of 20, because only an immensely stupid gang of neonates would consider something like that a good idea.<br /> <br /> If you're going to artificially construct the scenario necessary to make it a threat, of course it's a threat. But that sounds more like a problem of a jerk Storyteller than a reasonable interpretation of the World of Darkness as presented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T08:38:12-07:00","id":1465144,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a>, this is simply not how vampires behave in the setting as written. Such behavior would just get all vampires dead in no time. But that does explain some of your posts.<br /> <br /> Vampires are calculating manipulators. They don't simply grab you by force and shove blood down your mouth, even because that would also make a very shitty Blood Bond. Is a bonded Mage a valuable asset? Sure. But from this to a vampire actually trying to identify a Mage, finding one, deciding to really go forward with the idea, prepping it and finally trying to pull it out, it will be a long, long road. And it probably will be through cunning and not by force-feeding you as that is incredibly risky and vampires hate risk, not to say it throws up most of your value out of the window.<br /> <br /> You have a very skewed view of how vampires behave, in many levels. I'm not sure where this came from and it isn't wrong for your game or anything, it just isn't the default most of us will take for granted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:43:33-07:00","id":1465198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465098#post1465098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before dark if they're smart, if you're going to propose a non-standard setting where Mages are artificially weakened and Vampires are unusually aggressive.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465098#post1465098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize this is probably where there has been something of a misunderstanding. You had initially posed this hypothetical scenario of Arete-1-only Mages-in-a-Vampire-gangland back on the previous page. I wasn't really thinking of that specifically when responding, but more the general idea of roving gangs of Vampires being a threat that a Mage would typically have to consider.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Vampire gangland aspect can legitimately be attributed to me with my subjective, experience-based interpretation of how Vampires act (also based on statements of members in other posts about Vamps and Mages). The suggestion that starting Mages would have Arete 1 or 2 came from <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1464882#post1464882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure a Vampire Neonate is in trouble if he messes with a couple of Mages of Arete 3-4 or a Master Mage. But if we're talking about a Vampire Neonate, then maybe she or he should be compared to Arete 1-2 Mages. And such Mages, well...one certainty they have is that they can run back to their Chantry <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . Or try to stall for time by showing some nice Magick. Changing colors of items with Matter, influencing card draws or dice rolls with Entropy...might just make a Kindred consider a Mage differently.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465098#post1465098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the conditions imposed, I'm inclined to agree that the deck is stacked against the Mages in a straight-up conflict; it was just a page or so back that I made a little &quot;tier list&quot; that had beginner Mages come out behind beginner Vampires, especially if you're imposing restrictions on the power level of the Mages without any restrictions on the Vampires. It's trivially true, as is the follow-up that building Mage characters to survive in such a world would require some radically different considerations.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we agree that the deck would be stacked against the Mages under those conditions, there is another basic principle that applies; Weakness Inspires Aggression. If the Vampires stand to gain Mage-ghouls with little resistance, it's an appetizing proposition. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465098#post1465098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I would also mention the caveat that the deck is stacked against the Vampires in one particular regard: detection. Only a minority of beginner-level Vampires will possess Auspex, which is the only way a Vampire can recognize the difference between a Mage and a Sleeper unless they witness them using magic. And I think it was just a page or so back in this thread that it was being debated how effective that method is. In comparison, I can think of ways for nearly half of the level 1 Spheres to pick a Vampire out of a crowd; Life, Entropy, and Prime are pretty obvious, plus Time if you have a Vampire much older than its physical appearance would indicate, and Forces could likely detect their body being at room temperature, etc., etc. Limiting the Mages to only their sensory abilities and then precluding them any chance to use those abilities to avoid the conflict in the first place unbalances the whole thing significantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Mages have low Arete, they are limited to 1 success on their sensory roll, on average. With respectable Arete, they <i>would</i> have the jump on the Vamps. I think we both prefer the latter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465098#post1465098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just not the way typical Vampire/Mage crossover goes. Have you ever read the long screed about &quot;turning Vampires into lawn-chairs&quot; that was included in M20? It's been a while, but the big point that it hits on is that it's a very dumb idea for a lot of reasons unless the deck is already ridiculously stacked in your favour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a laugh reading this to my girlfriend, trying to explain - never mind (Tzimisce shit-stall).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465098#post1465098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Average Vampires habitually trying to blood-bond Mages is basically the reverse-lawnchair. Getting past the point I made about only a minority of Vampires being equipped to actively seek out Mages, it's the sort of thing that is only rarely going to happen because there will likely be horrible consequences for doing so; the potential of a vengeful master, of colleagues retaliating collectively to discourage precisely that kind of behaviour. If a Vampire is trying to blood-bond your Mage in a normal game of MtAs, you're not going to be dealing with a coterie of neonates, it's going to be an Elder or a Methuselah, 19 times out of 20, because only an immensely stupid gang of neonates would consider something like that a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will keep this in mind in any future discussions where someone casually says, &quot;Mages? Just blood-bond them.&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465144#post1465144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a>, this is simply not how vampires behave in the setting as written. Such behavior would just get all vampires dead in no time. But that does explain some of your posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This excerpt reflects my ideal version of a Mage/Vampire WoD setting: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1461796#post1461796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Milieus in which Vampires and Technocrats might meet and have common ground:<br /> <br /> - A Toreador architect meets an It-X Macrotechnician architect at a builders' conference. They are both passionate about building-aesthetics and skylines. Each tells the other a little about their Clan/Convention.<br /> <br /> - A Vampire with a Herd becomes interested in the ability of humans to recover from blood loss, replenish and produce more blood. He starts consulting people in the medical community and meets a Progenitor Mage equally interested in studying a willing Vampire test subject.<br /> <br /> - A competitive Lasombra Vampire wants to improve her chess so she can impress others in her Clan. She meets an It-X Statistician at a chess club. He is in the process of developing the most cutting edge chess learning software. She is more than happy to test it out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465144#post1465144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are calculating manipulators. They don't simply grab you by force and shove blood down your mouth, even because that would also make a very shitty Blood Bond. Is a bonded Mage a valuable asset? Sure. But from this to a vampire actually trying to identify a Mage, finding one, deciding to really go forward with the idea, prepping it and finally trying to pull it out, it will be a long, long road. And it probably will be through cunning and not by force-feeding you as that is incredibly risky and vampires hate risk, not to say it throws up most of your value out of the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was actually saying that the Coterie/Pack would have someone using Presence or Dominate and another with Celerity preventing the Mages from running away. Toreador and Brujah have Celerity and Presence as Clan Disciplines. A single Vampire could chase and Entrance. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465144#post1465144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have a very skewed view of how vampires behave, in many levels. I'm not sure where this came from and it isn't wrong for your game or anything, it just isn't the default most of us will take for granted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just repeat what I said in reply to <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>. The Vampire gangland aspect can legitimately be attributed to me with my subjective, experience-based interpretation of how Vampires act (also based on statements of members in other posts about Vamps and Mages).<br /> <br /> The Vampire Chronicles I have followed on YouTube portray sensible Kindred, but these are meant to appeal to a broader audience that might include Mage players. If it's really the case that the player base for Vampire are more sensible than those I have come across, it's good news for me, since I have unused crossover plots banked in my head; the subject of a future post. Consider my view adjusted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T17:04:35-07:00","id":1465212,"title":"","content":"Don't take hyperbole at face value, crossover posts aren't crossover games. Those are answers given in the context of threads usually filled with conflict, either by design or by disposition of the participants.<br /> <br /> On most games vampires won't act like that even with mortals. Unless they're fresh Sabbat shovelheads, but then they ARE dumb and not expected to live long, a week, tops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T10:34:06-07:00","id":1465293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465198#post1465198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Vampire gangland aspect can legitimately be attributed to me with my subjective, experience-based interpretation of how Vampires act (also based on statements of members in other posts about Vamps and Mages). The suggestion that starting Mages would have Arete 1 or 2 came from <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, and those users posts could be based on their own subjective experiences, if they primarily play Vampire and Mages are easily-beaten antagonists for their Storyteller, or if it's just crossover posturing that's fairly common when fans of different splats start smashing them together like action figures, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> suggested.<br /> <br /> But it's also worth pointing that Muad'Dib's &quot;1 or 2&quot; is already a significant step up from &quot;strictly 1,&quot; especially when I suspect they mean &quot;most Mages will have 1 or 2, because only a minority will invest the significant amount of freebies needed for 3.&quot; Assuming we're taking PC char-gen rather than random NPCs. But yes, while it's not necessarily a curbstomp, low-level Mages versus low-level Vampires is probably stacked in the Vampires favor in a straight-up fight, though really it's going to be more like Rock-Paper-Scissors depending on the respective builds. You can build a starting Mage with Arete 3, Forces 3 and Prime 2 that will be a serious threat to almost any Vampire, with M20 rules.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465198#post1465198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we agree that the deck would be stacked against the Mages under those conditions, there is another basic principle that applies; Weakness Inspires Aggression. If the Vampires stand to gain Mage-ghouls with little resistance, it's an appetizing proposition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weakness does inspire aggression, but that again only applies in a world where your Mages are artificially limited to 1 Arete and Level 1 Spheres. In a world where Mages exist with a vast range of power levels, Vampires flippantly hunting down Mages to try and blood-bond them do not have the means of detecting the Spheres or Arete level of a Mage, meaning that it will likely be a lot of work for them to figure out whether they're dealing with a vulnerable apprentice level Mage or a Hermetic Master of Forces that could turn them all to ash with a scowl. Vampires can get away with picking on low level Mages, but high-level Mages are terrifying, and to the extent that Vampire society knows about Mages, the general attend tends to be &quot;do NOT fuck with them unless you have a damn good reason.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's actually pretty common sense in World of Darkness that just picking a fight out of the blue is often a very bad idea, because the world is full of terrifying super-monsters hiding behind the face of Joe Average. Vampires are more aware of this than most because most Vampires can't even tell the 'power level' of their own kind just by looking at them. Attacking without having extensively scoped out a target first is potentially inviting a situation to blow up in your face, because you underestimated your target or you underestimated their connections. Of course, Vampires do have to attack random people out of the blue more than other supernaturals, and statistically that does get messy sometimes when they end up trying to jump another supernatural for blood. I imagine Bone Gnawers are a source of urban horror stories for Vampires.<br /> <br /> And to be clear, weakness inspiring aggression is likely going to be a factor in the instances where Vampires do try to blood-bond a Mage (I'll go into this a bit more below).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465198#post1465198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Mages have low Arete, they are limited to 1 success on their sensory roll, on average. With respectable Arete, they <i>would</i> have the jump on the Vamps. I think we both prefer the latter.</div> </div> </div> </div>If sensory abilities is all those Mages have, they're going to have every reason to try and get the most out of it. Which means using every possible method of lowering the Difficulty of their casting. They'll be limited to one success no matter what, but there's no reason to believe they'd be completely incapable of using their magic when they really need it. I don't know much about ritual casting, so maybe that's not possible at such a low level, but using a ritual to set up the Effect before they start their day/night may be an option. Though that may make them more susceptible to detection by Auspex.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465198#post1465198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will keep this in mind in any future discussions where someone casually says, &quot;Mages? Just blood-bond them.&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are some legitimate reasons why blood-bonding is a common suggestion Vampire players might make for handling something like Mages. It's the one method that nearly every Vampire possesses, no matter how lacking their are in social Disciplines, for turning a potential enemy into a minion. But there are limitations. In particular, the fact that a full blood-bond takes at least three nights to set up. Even if a Vampire manages to run down a Mage and force them to drink the first dose of vitae, that first-stage bond isn't going to be strong enough to compel the Mage to let the Vampire give them the second dose. They will have an entire day to respond, whether that means trying to run, trying to fight back, or seeking help from allies. Unless the Vampire kidnaps the Mage, in which case any allies they have will likely have questions about why they haven't heard from them for three days. Or the Vampire might be in the position to slip doses of vitae into the Mage's food or drink, but that could require a fair amount of effort to set up, especially if the Mage in question is appropriately paranoid.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, the most likely Mage to be targeted by Vampires for a Blood Bond is an isolated one. And a Vampire that has the means of determining whether or not a Mage is a safe target for an attempted blood-bond and then successfully dosing the Mage three times is not going to be a neonate, probably not even an ancilla. It's going to be an Elder or something more powerful, that has carefully vetted the target before making a move.<br /> <br /> Which isn't to say that neonates trying to jump a Mage isn't a thing. It's just something that ends badly for the Vampires more often than not. Mages make the best detectives, and they can operate during the day.<br /> <br /> Again, going off half-cocked in the World of Darkness is almost always a bad idea, because there is always a Bigger Fish.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465198#post1465198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was actually saying that the Coterie/Pack would have someone using Presence or Dominate and another with Celerity preventing the Mages from running away. Toreador and Brujah have Celerity and Presence as Clan Disciplines. A single Vampire could chase and Entrance.</div> </div> </div> </div>A coterie of Vampires versus one Mage is likely to go pretty bad for the Mage. But a coterie versus a cabal becomes much more of a dice roll due to the potential builds, as I noted above. A starter Mage with Forces 3 and Prime 2 is an extreme example, but even Forces 2 with a pre-existing source of flame would be a source of Rotschreck. Mind 1 allows for the creation of mental shields that would aid in resisting Dominate or Presence. If the Vampires don't subdue the entire cabal in their first strike, there's a lot of potential for chaos. Which again invites the question, does the coterie really want to risk everything on a crapshoot? And if they've spent the time and done the work to make sure that it *isn't* a crapshoot, I'd argue that they deserve it, or conversely that the Mages deserve it for not covering their arses better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:57:48-07:00","id":1465311,"title":"","content":"It seems to me if you are a Mage, and you only have Arete 1, that you would still be able to detect things like vampires and do so coincidentally, and having done so make sure you stay the hell away from them. Take advantage of your cabal and chantry for protection and knowledge. Stay alert and don't get involved in things you can't handle. Such a novice Mage is probably indistinguishable from an ordinary person. There should not be any reason why any vampire is searching specifically for you, so the Mage should have the advantage in remaining anonymous and avoid trouble. Only later when the Mage has improved his knowledge and can do much more, would he even risk interacting with any vampire.<br /> <br /> In terms of the Technocracy itself, they probably have so much surveillance and assets that they'd be able to protect the vast majority of their members from inadvertently stumbling across something. You're not dealing with a specific cabal or chantry here, but the entire organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T13:12:20-07:00","id":1465315,"title":"","content":"I think it is a good moment to explain more about the Blood Bond for <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26467_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26467\" data-vbnamecard=\"26467\">HorizonParty2021</a> and anyone else that may want this info to use vampires in interesting ways. Going as RAW:<br /> <br /> The first thing a Vampire must do is make the target drink the blood. Any amount of blood does the trick, but sometimes it ends up being a full Blood Point, which means a loss for the Vampire and a gain for the Bonded.<br /> <br /> With this, two effects happen to a mortal, including a Mage: first, the First Level of the Bond sets in. This is a weak emotional effect, the Bonded will think about the vampire frequently, even if they never saw the Kindred before, but that's it. There are no rules, the bonded acts on these flourishing emotions as they see fit.<br /> <br /> Second, and this is important, <b><u>the victim turns into a Ghoul</u></b>. Even without a full BP the victim immediately gains a full <b>dot of Potency </b>to play with. Any full BP can be used for healing and stuff.<br /> <br /> No amount of blood will affect the strength of the Bond in a single night, no matter if concentrated or spread through several doses, so only from the next night on the Kindred may try to increase it to Level 2, in the exactly same way. A Level 2 Bond does cause strong emotions, enough for the Kindred to become an important person in your life. Mechanically, though, it is only two effects, the Kindred have -1 dif on social rolls against you and you must roll Willpower if you want to directly harm the Kindred. But otherwise you're free to act as you will, and the emotions are strong but not dissociated of context. If you're bonded after being physically assaulted, there is a good chance that you won't be happy with the Kindred.<br /> <br /> Finally comes the Level 3 Bond. It is an extremely strong love. In fact, emotionally speaking it is among the strongest forms of love possible. Everything else in your life becomes secondary to it. The 3rd level Bond immediately shatters every other lesser level Bond you have and immunizes you not just against other Bonds, but against <b>anything</b> that tries to interfere with this emotion. By RAW, not even a powerful Mind effect can force you to act against the Bond, it would have to Break the Bond itself to do so.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, though, the Bond have few hard rules. Your regnant have an easier time using Dominate on you, which is neat if they have Dominate to begin with. No need for eye contact and you get a +2 dif to resist if you try to. The main rule, though, is that to act against the Bond you'll have a pretty hard time, a Willpower roll dif 8 just to get the right to try, then spending willpower to go through it, with the level of &quot;treason&quot; defining how much time you can act against the Bond for each WP, going from 1 turn (direct attack) to 1 scene (send a letter to a rival).<br /> <br /> And that's it. The secret lies in the lack of details. What consists on &quot;acting against the Bond&quot; is undefined by design. It is a strong emotion, unnaturally strong, but actually quite natural on how it evolves. The Bond is a relationship, and nothing stops you from hating at the same time that you love. The only one able to dictate how you'll act when in love is yourself, and the Blood Bond doesn't actually makes it less true, so much so that even for common mortals the rules strongly recommend for the ST to take in consideration the Nature of the Bonded.<br /> <br /> Vampires that take no care with the Bond may end up with thralls that hunt and kill the Kindred's other servants out of jealousy, or protective lovers that sabotage their plans and communications &quot;for their protection and happiness&quot;. A Mind Mage could reasonably decide to use Magic to <b>make</b> those feelings be reciprocated, and a thrall that hates you can easily wait for the right moments to make those WP expenditures for maximum effect.<br /> <br /> Blood Bonds are the most powerful readily available weapon in a vampire's arsenal, and one of the few potent enough to threaten anything else as its formation can't be resisted. But without a lot of care this weapon backfires. A lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T23:47:11-07:00","id":1465361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1458960-what-do-vampires-know-if-anything-about-the-technocracy?p=1465315#post1465315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blood Bonds are the most powerful readily available weapon in a vampire's arsenal, and one of the few potent enough to threaten anything else as its formation can't be resisted. But without a lot of care this weapon backfires. A lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangent: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r5oOq4S4tbM\" target=\"_blank\">An example of what a high-Rage Garou with a level 3 bond might act like</a>.<br /> <br /> More toward substance, Bringers of Light can break the bond, but it's a level 5 Gift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T04:38:28-07:00","id":1465378,"title":"","content":"One thing I forgot to mention, the Will roll to get to expend WP at a Level 3 Bond must gather as much successes as the times you fed from the regnant before. V20 don't mention more, the rule used to be different with the number of times you feed affecting difficulty and V20 kept it as a typo, so there is a limit, but undefined. Without looking at old rules I would recommend 5 successes as the limit, unless you decide that it can be done as an extended action, which then could have a far higher limit.<br /> <br /> In the end, ways of getting rid of the Bond exist, but are rare and powerful. Bringers of Light is actually a Camp, the only one that can learn the Gift <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> mentioned, Purity of Blood, that not only is Level 5, but must be taught to a member of the Camp by an avatar of Grandfather Thunder in person.<br /> <br /> For Mage I'd rule something with high levels of Mind, Entropy and Prime, at least one at 5, Quintessence expenditure and lots of successes (at least 10, preferably 15+), and even then only by a Mage that went through the Bond once, so they know what it is really like, or some other event-like requisite.<br /> <br /> The Bond can be broken with a lot of effort, usually by abstaining from contact with the regnant for years, which in itself counts as going against the Bond. The rule of thumb is (12 - Willpower) months for each stage, but a Full Bond retains full effect until the last stage is broken, so three times that amount. A Willpower 10 Mage will still have to withstand 6 months without contact with the person they love the most in the world. Poignant, but perfectly doable.<br /> <br /> Why I wouldn't recommend making it easier to resist or break? Because that would take out the sting completely. With the actual level of freedom the Bond offers to the player of the victim, the thing that makes it interesting is the very notion of this emotional nuclear option, messed up and chaotic, but unavoidable as a force of nature, and so sensitive to how you manage to cause it and to whom. Dominate is more reliable at every turn, even if easier to break, heck, offering money for service is more reliable than the Blood Bond. If you don't want the unstoppable Bond in your game it is better to just use Disciplines and scrap the effect completely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}